 ## Background
-Ray Marching Particle Grid Traversal was developed as part of a WebGPU-based voxel cone tracing and particle rendering system. The technique was documented in an unofficial GitHub repository by Hector Arellano Dev, which provides a complete implementation of the algorithm in WebGPU shaders [S1, unofficial]. The optimization of reading contiguous rows of cells as ranges was further discussed in a pull request by Siroko for the "kansei" project, which highlighted performance gains in ray-traced lightbox rendering [S2, unofficial]. The method is distinct from traditional grid-based volume rendering as it focuses on discrete particle spheres rather than continuous scalar fields [S1, unofficial].
+Ray Marching Particle Grid Traversal was developed as part of a WebGPU-based voxel cone tracing and particle rendering system [S1, unofficial]. The technique was documented in an unofficial GitHub repository by Hector Arellano Dev, which provides a complete implementation of the algorithm in WebGPU shaders [S1, unofficial]. The optimization of reading contiguous rows of cells as ranges was further discussed in a pull request by Siroko for the "kansei" project, which highlighted performance gains in ray-traced lightbox rendering [S2, unofficial]. The method is distinct from traditional grid-based volume rendering as it focuses on discrete particle spheres rather than continuous scalar fields [S1, unofficial].
 
